  {
   "id": "fwZZEvtmAwAJ",
   "from": "Paul Buerkner",
   "author": "6e3dd74b422c061b",
   "date": "2017-09-09T18:45:14Z",
   "subject": "Re: [brms-users] priors for bernoulli model",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"auto\">Not sure if the flat prior is most appropriate, but a wide normal prior will likely leed to the same posterior. It is hard to tell when a prior matters, and it depends certainly on the prior itself as well. Maybe just try it out and get a feeling of its influence for your data?</div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">Am 09.09.2017 20:19 schrieb &quot;Paul Lantos&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">paul....@gmail.com</a>&gt;:<br type=\"attribution\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Thanks - I guess a more complicated issue is that the outcome probability varies over space (which is the point of putting in the s(long, lat) term to begin with. So does that suggest a flat prior is the most appropriate for the intercept? Or would I do something like a normal prior over the average of the intercept and keep it loose enough to encompass the high and low extremes of error?</div><div><br></div><div>Most of my data sets are in the 100s to 1000s of observations (this one is particularly large). With say 1000 observations am I still in the territory where the priors wouldn&#39;t make much of an impact?</div><div><br><br>On Saturday, September 9, 2017 at 2:02:24 PM UTC-4, Paul Buerkner wrote:</div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;padding-left:1ex;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-width:1px;border-left-style:solid\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>The Intercept has an improper flat prior over the reals by default.</div><div><br></div><div>The student_t(3, 0, 10) prior you mention refers to the standard deviation parameter of the s(long, lat) spline.</div><div><br></div><div>Also, you have to keep in mind that all the coefficients are on the logit scale, so it is actually more complicated to reformulate your knowledge about the prevalance into a prior for the Intercept.</div><div><br></div><div>A prevalance of 2% would translate to a value of roughly -3.9 on the logit scale, so maybe one could use this information in the prior by using a normal prior centered around -3.9 for the Intercept.</div><div><br></div><div> However, I don&#39;t think it will change the posterior by much as long as you don&#39;t make the prior too narrow, which you probably don&#39;t want to do anyway.</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Paul<br></div></div><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">2017-09-09 19:36 GMT+02:00 Paul Lantos <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">paul....@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span>:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;padding-left:1ex;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-width:1px;border-left-style:solid\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi Paul,</div><div> I&#39;ve been using default priors for my current models. The default is a student_T(3, 0, 10) on the intercept.</div><div><br></div><div> However, I was wondering if I should provide more informative priors. The &quot;prior&quot; information for the disease I&#39;m studying is that it has a prevalence of 0.001 to 0.003 depending on the studied population. In my dataset the prevalence is about 10 times higher, but still, it&#39;s only around 0.02 to 0.05.</div><div><br></div><div> So it seems I could constrain the model to a more realistic prior probability range - for instance a prior prevalence between 0 and 0.05 or 0 and 0.1 would be more realistic than 0 to 1.</div><div><br></div><div> It may not matter since I have a lot of observations (nearly 20,000), but it&#39;s probably at least worth testing. How would you recommend changing the prior to account for this more realistic prior information?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div>Paul</div><div><br></div><div>Here&#39;s an example of a model with a few covariates -</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"margin:0px;background-color:white\"><font face=\"Calibri,sans-serif\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;background-color:white\"><font color=\"black\" face=\"Lucida Console\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Lucida Console,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\">Family: bernoulli(logit) </span></font></span></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;background-color:white\"><font face=\"Calibri,sans-serif\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;background-color:white\"><font color=\"black\" face=\"Lucida Console\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Lucida Console,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\">Formula: Result ~ s(long, lat) + race + CMV_neg + CMV_pos </span></font></span></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;background-color:white\"><font face=\"Calibri,sans-serif\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;background-color:white\"><font color=\"black\" face=\"Lucida Console\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Lucida Console,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\"> </span></font></span></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;background-color:white\"><font face=\"Calibri,sans-serif\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;background-color:white\"><font color=\"blue\" face=\"Lucida Console\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Lucida Console,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\">&gt; prior_summary(Model5)</span></font></span></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;background-color:white\"><font face=\"Calibri,sans-serif\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;background-color:white\"><font color=\"black\" face=\"Lucida Console\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Lucida Console,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\">                prior     class         coef group nlpar bound resp dpar</span></font></span></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;background-color:white\"><font face=\"Calibri,sans-serif\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;background-color:white\"><font color=\"black\" face=\"Lucida Console\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Lucida Console,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\">1                             b                                         </span></font></span></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;background-color:white\"><font face=\"Calibri,sans-serif\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;background-color:white\"><font color=\"black\" face=\"Lucida Console\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Lucida Console,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\">2                             b      CMV_neg                            </span></font></span></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;background-color:white\"><font face=\"Calibri,sans-serif\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;background-color:white\"><font color=\"black\" face=\"Lucida Console\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Lucida Console,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\">3                             b      CMV_pos                            </span></font></span></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;background-color:white\"><font face=\"Calibri,sans-serif\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;background-color:white\"><font color=\"black\" face=\"Lucida Console\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Lucida Console,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\">4                             b RaceMinority                            </span></font></span></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;background-color:white\"><font face=\"Calibri,sans-serif\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;background-color:white\"><font color=\"black\" face=\"Lucida Console\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Lucida Console,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\">5                             b   slonglat_1                            </span></font></span></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;background-color:white\"><font face=\"Calibri,sans-serif\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;background-color:white\"><font color=\"black\" face=\"Lucida Console\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Lucida Console,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\">6                             b   slonglat_2                            </span></font></span></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;background-color:white\"><font face=\"Calibri,sans-serif\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;background-color:white\"><font color=\"black\" face=\"Lucida Console\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Lucida Console,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\">7                     Intercept                                         </span></font></span></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;background-color:white\"><font face=\"Calibri,sans-serif\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;background-color:white\"><font color=\"black\" face=\"Lucida Console\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Lucida Console,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\">8 student_t(3, 0, 10)       sds                                         </span></font></span></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;background-color:white\"><font face=\"Calibri,sans-serif\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;background-color:white\"><font color=\"black\" face=\"Lucida Console\" size=\"2\" style=\"font-family:Lucida Console,serif,&quot;EmojiFont&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\">9                           sds  s(long,lat)     </span></font></span></font></div></div></div><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message becau